# What reaches huvudkontoret.io.
#
# The asset directory is the repo root, so without this file the whole
# checkout is served — agent instructions, design docs, the gate's own source.
# That is what GitHub Pages does today: https://huvudkontoret.io/CLAUDE.md
# answers 200 text/markdown. Everything listed here stops being part of the
# site. Nothing is hidden by it; the repo stays public on GitHub.
#
# Published: index.html, index.md, llms.txt, llms-full.txt, robots.txt,
# sitemap.xml, .well-known/ and assets/. The gate asserts that list is exactly
# what survives, so a new file added to the repo root cannot quietly appear on
# the site — see tools/check/checks/workers.mjs.

# Source, not site. `src/` holds the chrome layer the perspectives will be
# built from — profile.css is a stylesheet the site never links, because .io
# carries the same properties inline (ADR 0004). It goes away with this whole
# file once the asset directory becomes dist/, where only the built site
# exists in the first place.
src/

# Repo scaffolding
.claude/
.editorconfig
.githooks/
.github/
.gitignore
.prettierrc
.vscode/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md
README.md
docs/
hk.json
tools/
tsconfig.json
wrangler.jsonc
.assetsignore

# GitHub Pages leftovers. Kept in the repo until the cutover to Workers is
# verified — removing them early would strip Pages of its custom domain while
# it is still serving the apex.
CNAME
.nojekyll

# Not linked from anywhere on the site.
demo-hero.html

# MonoLisa is purchased and the web licence is not confirmed, so the woff2
# files are gitignored. Wrangler uploads the working directory rather than the
# git tree, so a local `wrangler deploy` would publish them anyway — this is
# the only thing that stops it. Remove this together with the .gitignore rule,
# never on its own. See assets/fonts/README.md.
assets/fonts/*.woff2

# Local noise that is never part of the site.
.DS_Store
